ANARI significantly simplifies the development of applications in domains such
as scientific visualization by providing high-level functionality to build an
in-memory scene representation to be rendered without need for low-level
graphics code, and enabling the use of any 3D rendering engine that supports the
ANARI API. ANARI has already been widely integrated into scientific
visualization applications, and is expected to be used by diverse applications
needing portable access to multiple rendering engines delivering sophisticated
3D functionality such as ray tracing and global illumination.
